id: pm-memory-native-revision-foundation
title: SDK revision foundation and native verification
description: "Part 1 of the accepted PR #15 split plan. Extract SDK-normalized document and immutable history proofs, bind verification to a frozen native snapshot, recheck the SDK pre-write hook and validate no-ops. Keep portable manifests and merge-receipt migration outside this change. Related items: pm-memory-1363 and pm-memory-c3gv."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: "gh:unbraind/pm-memory#30","related:pm-memory-1363","related:pm-memory-c3gv"
created_at: "2026-10-30T23:59:27.944Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T01:33:40.170Z"
author: codex-agent
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-memory-1363,related,"2026-10-31T00:03:23.077Z",codex-agent,"cli:update:dep",detected
  pm-memory-c3gv,related,"2026-10-31T00:03:23.077Z",codex-agent,"cli:update:dep",detected
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-30T23:59:30.856Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator accepted split part 1 only. New branch starts from origin/main. Original worktree remains clean at 33c550e and PR #15 remains unchanged. Main already provides lease/fence helpers; extract only SDK schema/revision primitives and verification changes. Carry real non-git tracker controls for native collisions, independent peers, complete-hash ABA, permissions, unchanged snapshots and SDK no-ops. Preserve coverage thresholds and 0% duplication; run full npm and Bun release gates serially at two workers maximum. Related umbrella pm-memory-1363 and recovery blocker pm-memory-c3gv remain outside this implementation."
  "2026-10-31T00:29:48.277Z",codex-agent,"Extraction-specific revert proof 1: in a disposable copy, only commitNativeFields was changed to perform the same fenced SDK update without revision/pre-write/no-op guards. Command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/native-revision.test.ts test/verification-collision.test.ts. Result: 19 failed, 4 passed, zero canceled/skipped. Independent native writers and collision cases expose invalid publication. Fixed implementation restored in finally."
  "2026-10-31T00:29:50.549Z",codex-agent,"Extraction-specific revert proof 2: only sameNativeProof was weakened to compare the complete content hash while ignoring immutable history. Same two-file command: 3 failed, 20 passed, zero canceled/skipped. The history-component control and real identical-content ABA fail. Fixed implementation restored in finally."
  "2026-10-31T00:29:52.806Z",codex-agent,"Extraction-specific revert proof 3: only observeTargets was changed to adopt current SDK state without binding the supplied corpus digest. Command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/native-revision-capture.test.ts. Result: 1 failed, 2 passed, zero canceled/skipped. A different native body with the same updated_at is wrongly adopted. Fixed implementation restored in finally."
  "2026-10-31T00:29:54.934Z",codex-agent,"Extraction-specific revert proof 4: only verify was restored from origin/main. Command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/verification-collision.test.ts. Result: 12 failed, 6 passed, zero canceled/skipped. Fixed implementation restored in finally. Final restored command across native-revision-capture, native-revision and verification-collision test files: 26/26 passed. No reviewed worktree source was mutated for these proofs. Previous-release must-allow fixture was generated by verified public pm-memory@2026.10.28 with the pinned SDK; only synthetic text records and archive provenance are tracked."
  "2026-10-31T00:55:50.125Z",codex-agent,"Full serial release gates passed with isolated home and credential-free child environments: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 303/303 suite tests plus 2/2 packed-consumer checks, zero failures/canceled/skipped. Both measured 100/100/100/100 statement/branch/function/line coverage across 27 source files and 0% duplication (0/8715 lines, zero clone pairs, 72 sources). Typecheck, lint, documented declarations, production audit, packing, changelog and publish-attestation checks passed. Every test launcher is capped at two workers; no thresholds or dependency pins changed. SDK revision controls use real non-git trackers. Existing main histories and the original candidate worktree remain unchanged; dist is ignored and rebuilt by both gates."
  "2026-10-31T00:57:02.828Z",codex-agent,"Opened part-1 PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/30 with acceptance/evidence table, all four behavioral revert proofs, and npm/Bun gate counts. Implementation commit: 6b3f0af. Strict pm health with required merge drivers exited 0; history drift and integrity passed, with one advisory local telemetry queue entry retained unchanged. Identity and changelog checks passed after the code commit. The final tracker receipt will carry the PR tag and release this author's claim before exact-head CI verification. CI and CodeQL results will be reported on the PR and in the final handoff, with a maximum sixty-minute wait on the final pushed head. Part 2 and part 3 remain under #15; no portable manifest, migration or legacy recovery implementation is included. No SDK capability gap or blocking part-1 risk was found."
  "2026-10-31T01:04:33.404Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CodeQL and Node 22 CI passed on 6acbe05. Final test audit found that independent peer controls exercised both publication boundaries but did not force equal native timestamps at those two boundaries. Strengthen the peer controls to use the saved native timestamp, add isolated boundary-only timestamp-revert proofs, then rerun both complete release gates and exact-head CI. This changes test strength, not implementation scope; #15 remains untouched."
  "2026-10-31T01:06:16.442Z",codex-agent,"Boundary-only revert proof 5: independent SDK peers now force updated_at equal to the saved native revision at BOTH publication boundaries. In a disposable copy, only commitNativeFields' pre-write hook comparison was weakened to diagnostic timestamp equality; initial capture, the initial full revision check and no-op guard were retained. Exact command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/native-revision.test.ts. Result: 1 failed, 4 passed, zero canceled/skipped; the pre-write peer collision was wrongly accepted. Fixed implementation restored in finally."
  "2026-10-31T01:06:19.308Z",codex-agent,"Boundary-only revert proof 6: in the same disposable copy, only commitNativeFields' SDK no-op read-back was weakened to diagnostic timestamp equality; initial capture, initial full revision check and the full pre-write hook remained fixed. Exact command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/native-revision.test.ts. Result: 1 failed, 4 passed, zero canceled/skipped; the colliding peer edit was wrongly accepted after an SDK no-op. Fixed implementation restored in finally. Both strengthened controls also pass against the fixed package worktree (5/5 focused tests)."
  "2026-10-31T01:06:31.549Z",codex-agent,"After both boundary-only reverts were restored in finally, the combined command node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/native-revision-capture.test.ts test/native-revision.test.ts test/verification-collision.test.ts passed 26/26, zero failed/canceled/skipped. This includes fixed timestamp collisions at capture, the real SDK pre-write hook, and SDK no-op read-back, plus complete-hash ABA, unchanged snapshot, permissions and published-record compatibility controls. The implementation is unchanged; complete release gates are being repeated for the stronger final tests."
  "2026-10-31T01:33:37.764Z",codex-agent,"Final stronger controls passed complete serial gates again: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 303/303 suite tests plus 2/2 packed npm/Bun consumer checks, with zero failed/canceled/skipped. Both retained 100/100/100/100 S/B/F/L coverage across 27 source files and 0% duplication (0/8718 lines, zero clone pairs, 72 sources). Typecheck, lint, docstrings, production audit, packing, changelog and publish-attestation checks passed; no retries or timeouts were needed. All six behavioral revert proofs are recorded above; restored controls pass 26/26. Product implementation remains unchanged from 6b3f0af; the final amendment strengthens independent native peer timestamp-collision tests and documents them. Release this author's claim, commit all tracker receipts, then verify CI and CodeQL on that final pushed head. Part 2/3 and original PR #15 remain unchanged; no blocking part-1 risk or SDK gap was found."
